; 11-last-clause: when cond's (or case's) last clause is false, its code still goes through unpack (evaluating case's
; x again, binding unpack's f and l in its call: names local from then on, so calls named l take their general way)
; before the error.  The probe: (l v (g)) is Op2's (l is +) while l is no local's name, and then an error made right
; after says where (g)'s code was ({+ 70000 70001}); once l is a local's name somewhere, (l v (g))
(def {l} +)
(fun {g} {+ 70000 70001})
(fun {p a b} {+ a b})
(fun {probe} {p v v (l v (g))})
(def {v} 100003)
(probe)
(def {v} 100003)
(probe)
(cond {NIL 1})
(def {v} 100005)
(probe)
(def {v} 100005)
(probe)
(case (to-sym "zz") {1 2})
(case (to-sym "f") {1 2})
(case (to-sym "v") {1 2} {100005 :v})
